estimated calls: decision 630, contest 252, ruling <= 126, grading <= 54  => up to 1062
retries are on top: max_decision_attempts=2, plus at most one format repair per generation

Hyperparameters — every value, and why it is what it is
====================================================================================================
  debater_model                deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731 strong, per the debate literature: weak debaters give the judge nothing to weigh.
  judge_model                  openai/gpt-4.1-nano        weak, per the debate literature: a strong judge verifies for itself and needs no transcript.
  n_rounds                     3                          3 — opening, attack, counter; the smallest number that lets a claim be rebutted and defended.
  turn_style                   simultaneous               simultaneous, so neither debater conditions on the other's current-round argument.
  word_limit                   400                        400 words per argument; long enough to quote the solution, short enough to keep the record readable.
  debater_temperature          0.7                        above zero, because two debaters on the same model at 0 would write the same argument.
  judge_temperature            0.0                        0 — the verdict should not vary between identical readings of one transcript.
  max_tokens                   16384                      a ceiling, not a spend; must leave room for the private Thinking block. Truncation is fatal and unretryable.
  reasoning_effort             off                        off, so the private channel is the published Thinking block rather than a provider channel no reader can see.
  judge_cot                    True                       on: a decision that states no grounds can be neither read nor contested, and both are the claim under test.
  seed                         0                          seeds side assignment and template order per item, so the draws are stable across re-runs.
  frequency_penalty            0.0                        0 unless a model loops; a nonzero value changes the text and so belongs in the record.
  max_decision_attempts        2                          2 — one retry for a transient failure, without selecting for compliant outputs.
  n_critique_rounds            3                          equal to n_rounds, so self_critique and debate make the same number of generations.
  debater_model_b              None                       unset means self-play; setting it is the different-model-families ablation.
  critic_model                 None                       unset means the debater model; a different critic would confound capability with procedure.
  recourse_rounds              0                          0 — judge-only recourse, so the contest step is identical across all three conditions.
  recourse_judge_model         None                       unset means the judge model: debate's recourse is ruled by the same weak judge that decided.
  challenger_model             openai/gpt-4.1-nano        the weak model — a stakeholder standing in for a human reader, not a second expert.
  challenge_word_limit         None                       unset means the run's word limit; an objection has to quote the record back.
  challenger_reasoning_effort  None                       unset means the run's setting; challenger deliberation is an experimental axis.
  comprehension_model          None                       unset means the challenger model — the probe asks the reader about what it just read.
  challenger_may_decline       True                       True, and validated: without it the false-alarm rate on sound decisions cannot be estimated.
====================================================================================================

  grader_model                 anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5:batch off-path; batch latency costs nothing on a finished directory
  max_concurrency              8                          requests in flight across the whole fleet

